{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "JnygO",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Activos",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "WpnvG",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Activos — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "B73zD0",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The 'Activos' tab — three tiers of interest in a symbol, drawn as a ladder (D9).\n\nRastreado (assets.sync_status active) → Sigo (watchlist_items) → Poseo (open positions). The tier is not taxonomy, it is BUDGET: SyncAllFundamentalsJob orders positions → watchlist → rest against DAILY_BUDGET = 25 calls/day, and only open positions get dividends + splits synced at all. The segmented control stays at two (the two daily questions); Rastreados is a foot-of-list entry with its own screen.\n\nEntry: bottom-nav 'Activos'. Rows link to the asset detail in cockpit.pen.\nScreens: Cartera · Sigo · Cartera vacía (first run) · Registrar movimiento (sheet) · Registrar movimiento con teclado (the real mobile spec, D11) · Rastreados · Rastreados·Buscar.\n\nGrounding: positions (shares, avg_cost, market_value, total_gain, cost_basis_in(MXN) via fx_rate_at_execution) · watchlist_items.entry_price captured on add → 'sigues +X%' (nothing renders it today) · assets (current_price, change_percent_24h, currency, exchange, asset_type, price_updated_at, sync_status) · latest_trend_score → the semáforo dots. You can only follow what is already rastreado: search hits `assets`, so the search screen IS the catalogue browser.\n\nCETES rows drop the sparkline and the semáforo — technical lights don't apply to fixed income — and carry days-to-maturity + annual rate instead (C1 Lucía).\n\nMoney per D10: the section header declares the currency, rows drop the symbol; off-currency values keep the ISO prefix (USD 172.40).\n\nDesktop (D4): reflows to a centered max-w list; the sheet becomes the same <dialog> centered. No separate artboard.\n\n⚠ Touch targets: segmented controls, rows and the keypad clear 44pt; filter chips sit at ~35pt + 8pt gap — below the floor, accepted for a secondary control, flagged rather than hidden.\n\nFlow-local components (kit candidates, not promoted): WatchRow, Segmented, OptionCard, TierChip, and the `scrim` token — see ui-kit.CHANGELOG 0.3.0 gaps.\n\nCopy: es-MX. kit-version-source 0.2.0.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
